## Legal Citations
- **Directive 2002/58/EC (ePrivacy Directive) (Article 5(3))**: Storing information, or gaining access to information stored, in terminal equipment requires affirmative consent. *[Sanction: GDPR Art. 83 fines up to €20M or 4% of global turnover.]*
- **Court of Justice of the European Union (CJEU) (Case C-673/17 (Planet49 GmbH))**: Pre-ticked checkboxes or implicit consent are legally invalid.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: NEVER load tracking pixels, cookies, or font CDNs prior to affirmative user consent.
- MUST: Decouple ePrivacy terminal storage consent from GDPR Art. 6 processing lawful bases.
- MUST: Provide symmetric Accept and Reject controls with equal visual prominence.
- MUST: Record consent with immutable audit logs and version hashes.
- MUST: Support instantaneous withdrawal under GDPR Art. 7(3).

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: <input type="checkbox" defaultChecked /> in consent modals
- NEVER: document.cookie = "tracking=true" without prior consent verification

## Reference Compliant Code Snippets
### Consent Gate Pattern
```tsx
import { EPrivacyConsentEngine, EPrivacyPurpose } from '@complirules/primitives';

export async function AnalyticsGate({ children, subjectId }: { children: React.ReactNode; subjectId: string }) {
  const allowed = await consentEngine.checkConsent(subjectId, EPrivacyPurpose.ANALYTICS);
  if (!allowed.allowed) return null;
  return <>{children}</>;
}
```
